  "full_text": "So, like, the Catholics say you pray to, like, saints and shit and Mary and stuff like that. So, I don't know. Like, if you want to do that, you can do that, I guess. Like, oh, I'm not going to bug Mr. God. I got no use for them saints and shit, I know. There are plenty of angels and shit, man. I just fucking talk, and God only knows how the fuck shit works, because that might be like praying and shit, man. Angels would be listening, and like, oh my God. People would declare avoidance and shit like that. So like, I don't know, but anyway. So like, here's the Catholic theology on Mary. Okay, all you women, you can pray to Mary, and she'll intercede and change God's mind, right? So let's just think about this. So, like, I'm talking to Mr. God, and he says, yeah, I sunk those migrant ships. And then all of a sudden the Pope says, no, no, no, no, save the migrants. And I'm going, you piece of shit, Pope. Like, don't you love God? Like, what the fuck, man? No, no, no, save the migrants. So just imagine this going on for, like, centuries, right? Like, save the migrants. God said he divorced Mary. That's what he told me. It might be kind of a, like, I tell that to my brother Danny. He'd probably laugh. I used to love her, but I had to kill her. I used to love her. Anyway, so whatever. So.",
